menu "mcp-broker provider (mcpb_esp)"

    config MCPB_ESP_RX_BUFFER
        int "Receive buffer (bytes)"
        default 8192
        range 512 65536
        help
            Bounds the largest JSON-RPC message the device can receive in one
            WebSocket message. A larger one is refused with code 1009 and the
            connection reopened, never truncated. Also holds the HTTP upgrade
            request during the handshake. Static, allocated once.

    config MCPB_ESP_TX_BUFFER
        int "Reply buffer (bytes)"
        default 4096
        range 256 65536
        help
            The buffer the message handler writes its reply into. A tools/list
            with many tools or a large tool result needs more. Static.

    config MCPB_ESP_TASK_STACK
        int "Provider task stack (bytes)"
        default 6144
        range 3072 32768
        help
            The handler runs on this task, so size it for your JSON layer and
            tool implementations, not only for libmcpb (which needs under 1 KB
            on top of esp-tls).

    config MCPB_ESP_TASK_PRIORITY
        int "Provider task priority"
        default 5
        range 1 24

    config MCPB_ESP_TASK_CORE
        int "Provider task core (-1: any)"
        default -1
        range -1 1

    config MCPB_ESP_POLL_MS
        int "Poll timeout (ms)"
        default 200
        range 10 5000
        help
            How long one poll waits for a message before returning to drain
            the outbox and check the stop flag. Keep it well under the
            broker's provider heartbeat (30 s by default): the broker's ping
            is answered from inside the poll.

    config MCPB_ESP_MULTIPLEX
        bool "Build the multiplexed /providers endpoint (mcpb_mux.h)"
        default n
        help
            Several provider slots on one socket, for a firmware that hosts
            more than one MCP server. Off, the two source files behind it are
            not compiled at all and the image carries none of it; a device
            with one provider uses the dedicated path and leaves this off.
            The provider task in mcpb_esp.h always uses the dedicated path;
            this option makes mcpb_mux_t available to an application that
            runs its own loop.

    config MCPB_ESP_TX_QUEUE_LEN
        int "Outbox depth (messages)"
        default 8
        range 1 64
        help
            Messages queued with mcpb_esp_send from other tasks, waiting for
            the provider task to send them. mcpb_esp_send fails with
            ESP_ERR_NO_MEM when it is full.

endmenu
